.TH MVM 1 "2026-11-25" "mvm 0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mvm \- run dev tooling in throwaway Podman+krun microVMs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mvm fetch
.RB [ go | rust | node ]
.RB [ \-\-learn ]
.RB [ \-\-
.IR CMD ...]
.br
.B mvm build
.RB [ go | rust | node ]
.RB [ \-w
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-it ]
.B \-\-
.IR CMD ...
.br
.B mvm run \-i
.I IMAGE
.RB [ \-u
.IR USER ]
.RB [ \-p
.IR HOST:CONT ]
.RB [ \-w
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-it ]
.B \-\-
.IR CMD ...
.br
.B mvm check
.RB [ \-\-all ]
.br
.B mvm status
.br
.BI "mvm pull " IMAGE
.br
.B mvm update
.br
.B mvm image build \-t
.IR localhost/NAME:TAG
.RB [ \-f
.IR FILE ]
.br
.B mvm cache
.BR rm " NAME | " grow " NAME SIZE | " gc
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mvm
runs package managers, compilers and tests inside a hardware-virtualized
microVM
.RB ( podman (1)
with
.BR "\-\-runtime krun" ),
with no host privileges.
.PP
.B fetch
is the only command that downloads (check reaches only api.osv.dev). It mounts a throwaway copy of the
dependency manifests only (go.mod, go.sum, go.work, Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock,
package.json, package\-lock.json; Cargo target files as empty stubs), never the
sources. Without
.I CMD
it runs
.BR "go mod download" ,
.BR "cargo fetch" " (\-\-locked when Cargo.lock exists)" " or"
.BR "npm ci \-\-ignore\-scripts \-\-no\-audit \-\-no\-fund"
for every ecosystem found in the current directory. With
.I CMD
it runs that command instead, to change dependencies
.RB ( "go get" ", " "cargo add" ", " "npm install" ).
Manifests that changed are copied back into the project and listed.
.PP
The fetch VM has no direct network. Its only way out is TCP to one
host\-loopback port, where a per\-run Smokescreen proxy (in a pod whose
kernel egress filter allows only TCP 443) allows only the
ecosystem's registries (plus
.B [allow]
from the config); DNS, other TCP, UDP, ICMP and IPv6 are closed. Each
connection and denial is logged in the run record and summarised.
.B \-\-learn
lets every host through but logs it, commits nothing, and prints the hosts
outside the allowlist. Without the proxy binary
.RI ( ~/.local/lib/mvm/smokescreen ", built by " "make smokescreen" ),
fetch refuses to run.
.PP
By default (off with
.BR "[observer] enabled = false" ),
mvm's own passive TLS sensor (stdlib Python) runs in the proxy pod and records
for each outbound connection whether it starts with a TLS ClientHello, its SNI,
JA4 and bytes in the run record. A TLS name outside the allowlist, a ClientHello
without SNI, a connection that is not TLS, or conflicting retransmissions hold the
run (exit 3). The
observer fails closed: without its image
.RB ( "make observer" )
fetch refuses to run; a dead observer, kernel packet drops, or a proxy connection
without an observed flow commits nothing (exit 5).
.PP
Before every fetch,
.B osv\-scanner
(Google, OSV.dev) checks the lockfiles (go.mod, Cargo.lock, package\-lock.json)
in a microVM that sees only those files and reaches only api.osv.dev through
the same allowlist proxy. A package with an OSV
.B MAL\-
advisory (OpenSSF malicious packages) refuses the fetch (exit 6); known
vulnerabilities are printed and recorded but do not block. When a fetch
command changed the lockfile, the new one is checked before anything is
committed or copied back. A check that cannot complete refuses the fetch;
.B [check] before_fetch = false
turns the check off.
.B mvm check
runs the same check here,
.B mvm check \-\-all
for every project mvm has fetched or checked (the daily timer, see
.BR "make timer" ).
With
.B [notify] ntfy
set, trips (malicious packages, held runs, failed proxy or observer, failed
checks) are posted there.
.PP
.B build
runs offline in the current project, mounted read\-only at
.IR /src ,
with the ecosystem's caches: dependency caches read\-only, build caches and the
project's node_modules writable. The ecosystem is detected from the current
directory unless named.
.B run
does the same for any image, without caches.
.PP
In build and run, files and directories matching the mask list (default:
.IR ".git .env .env.* .envrc .npmrc .netrc .pypirc *.pem *.key id_rsa* id_ecdsa* id_ed25519*" )
are hidden: directories appear empty, files appear empty.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Before the command: also print each run's egress and observer details, the
scanner's output and the run record path.
.TP
.BI \-w " DIR"
Make
.I ./DIR
writable (created if missing; must be inside the project). Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-it
Interactive terminal.
.TP
.BI \-i " IMAGE"
Image for
.BR run .
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " \fIUSER\fR"
.B run
only: run the command as
.I USER
(a name from the image,
.IR UID ,
or
.IR UID:GID ),
e.g. for Chromium, whose sandbox refuses uid 0. The project is still owned by
guest root: that user needs it traversable (mode 755), and a
.B \-w
directory writable by it
.RB ( "chmod 777 DIR" " or " "podman unshare chown UID DIR" ).
Files it writes there are owned by a subordinate uid on the host (remove them with
.BR "podman unshare rm" ).
.B build
and
.B fetch
always run as guest root: they loop\-mount the caches.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-publish " \fIHOST:CONT\fR"
.B run
only, repeatable: serve the guest's port
.I CONT
on host
.RI 127.0.0.1: HOST
(also written
.IR 127.0.0.1:HOST:CONT ;
any other bind address is refused), e.g. a dev server. The microVM runs in a
.B \-\-network=none
pod, whose namespace has only loopback, so it can open no connection at all (internet,
DNS, LAN, tailnet, or the host). mvm listens on the host port and splices each
connection to a Unix socket that a read\-only, no\-capability sidecar in the pod
.RB ( portbridge.py ,
in the pinned observer image:
.BR "make observer" )
forwards to 127.0.0.1:\fICONT\fR. The server must listen on 0.0.0.0 or 127.0.0.1.
.SH CACHES AND COMMIT-ON-CLEAN
Caches are sparse ext4 image files in
.IR ~/.cache/mvm ,
loop\-mounted inside the guest:
go\-mod, go\-build, cargo\-reg, cargo\-git, cargo\-target, npm, and one
nm\-<project>\-<hash> per node project.
A writable cache is reflink\-copied for the run and replaces the cache
atomically only when the command exits 0. Failure, interruption or a crash
leaves the cache unchanged. Each commit increments the cache's generation.
Readers take a shared
.BR flock (2),
the writer an exclusive one.
.TP
.B mvm cache gc
Remove leftover run copies, kill microVMs whose mvm process died, drop
node_modules caches of deleted projects.
.TP
.BI "mvm cache grow " "NAME SIZE"
Grow a cache image (refused while in use).
.TP
.BI "mvm cache rm " NAME
Delete a cache image (refused while in use).
.SH IMAGES
The first use of an image tag pins it to its digest in
.IR ~/.local/state/mvm/pins.json ;
later runs use the digest.
.B mvm update
re\-pulls every pinned tag and reports changes;
.BI "mvm pull " IMAGE
pulls and pins one (the full name, registry included).
Every container mvm starts uses
.BR \-\-pull=never :
a pinned image missing locally fails the run instead of being fetched.
.PP
Pulls are confined like fetch: a static skopeo
.RB ( "make skopeo" )
is the only process of a microVM behind the egress proxy and observer, and
copies the image into a
.B dir:
layout under
.IR ~/.cache/mvm/pulls .
Only after a clean run does the host load it offline
.RB ( "podman pull dir:" ...,
which re\-checks every blob) and pin it by the digest of its platform
manifest; the download is then removed.
A registry outside the allowlist holds the pull (exit 3).
Built\-in registries: Docker Hub and GHCR; others with
.BR "[allow] pull" .
.PP
Pull connections go first to
.B l7proxy
.RB ( "make l7proxy" ),
chained in front of Smokescreen in the same pod. It terminates TLS with an ephemeral,
name\-constrained CA made in memory per run (the guest trusts only it) and allows only
GET and HEAD, with SNI, Host and the CONNECT host equal, to
.I /v2/
and
.IR /v2/<repository>/ ...
on the registry, a token scoped to pulling that repository, and blob URLs exactly as a
registry redirect named them. A refusal holds the pull (exit 3). Rules for other
registries:
.BR "[[l7.pull]]" " host, exact, prefix, scope (" {repo} " is replaced)."
.PP
.B mvm image build
runs
.BR "podman \-\-runtime krun build" :
every RUN step runs in a KVM microVM on the confined network of fetch (proxy, TCP 443
only, observer), allowing only OS package mirrors (Alpine, Debian; more with
.BR "[allow] image\-build" ).
The build context holds only the Containerfile. Missing base images are pulled
through the egress first, then the build runs with
.BR "\-\-pull=never \-\-no\-cache" .
The result gets the requested
.I localhost/
tag only after a clean run; otherwise the temporary image is deleted (exit 3, 4 or 5).
Base images are used by their pinned digest. ADD (except heredocs), RUN \-\-network, RUN \-\-security, a non\-default # escape and FROM with variables are refused.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mvm/config.toml
Optional:
.B mask
(list),
.B [images]
(go, rust, node),
.B [allow]
(go, rust, node: lists of extra hosts for fetch; pull: extra registry hosts; image\-build: extra OS mirrors),
.B [[l7.pull]]
(request rules for pulls: host, exact, prefix, scope),
.B [memory]
(go, rust, node, run),
.B [observer]
(enabled = true|false, default true; log = "/abs/path.jsonl", opt\-in: append every
flow with its ETA features and run id, kind and eco),
.B [check]
(before_fetch = true|false, default true),
.B [notify]
(ntfy = "https://ntfy.example/<topic>").
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/mvm/runs/
One JSON record per run (last 200); observed runs include per\-flow ETA features
(timestamps, packets each way, data ratio, ALPN, TLS version, SPLT), observe\-only.
The state directory is kept 0700.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/mvm/checks/
Last check result per project.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR MVM_CACHE_DIR ", " MVM_STATE_DIR ", " MVM_CONFIG
override the paths above.
.B MVM_VERBOSE=1
is the same as
.BR \-v .
.SH EXIT STATUS
The command's exit status; 2 for usage errors; 130 when interrupted;
3 when a fetch exited 0 but tried a host the proxy denied (the run is held,
nothing is committed or copied back); 4 when the egress proxy died mid\-run or
its log could not be read (nothing committed); 5 when the observer was on and
died mid\-run, its flows could not be read, the kernel dropped packets, or it missed a
connection the proxy made (nothing committed); 6 when a lockfile pins a package
with an OSV MAL\- advisory (fetch refused or nothing committed;
.B mvm check
exits 6); 1 when a check could not complete.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mvm fetch
mvm check \-\-all
mvm fetch go \-\- go get golang.org/x/net@latest
mvm fetch rust \-\- cargo generate\-lockfile
mvm build \-w build \-\- go build \-o build/app ./cmd/app
mvm build node \-\- npm rebuild
mvm run \-i docker.io/library/alpine:3.24 \-\- uname \-a
mvm run \-u 1000:1000 \-i docker.io/library/alpine:3.24 \-\- id
mvm run \-p 8080:80 \-i docker.io/library/nginx:alpine \-\- nginx \-g 'daemon off;'
mvm pull ghcr.io/astral\-sh/ruff:0.8.4\-alpine
mvm image build \-t localhost/jq:1 \-f Containerfile
.fi
.SH CAVEATS
podman's
.B \-\-tmpfs
is ignored under krun.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR podman\-run (1),
.BR flock (2)
